{
  "headline": "FDA lists ifosfamide injection as a current shortage first posted 2026-06-12 with no public signal at our plants",
  "headline_cites": ["E12", "E8", "E9", "E10", "E11"],
  "sentences": [
    {
      "text": "FDA's shortage list shows ifosfamide injection as Current with an initial posting date of 2026-06-12 and updates through October 2026 for Baxter Healthcare, Fresenius Kabi USA LLC, Hikma Pharmaceuticals USA Inc., and SteriMax Inc.",
      "cites": ["E12", "E8", "E9", "E10", "E11"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The shortage has been on FDA's list for 4 months as of 2026-10-21.",
      "cites": ["D7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Our three sites use Hikma's 50 mg/mL 60 mL vial (NDC 0143-9530-01) supplied from the THYMOORGAN PHARMAZIE GmbH plant named on the label.",
      "cites": ["E1", "E5", "E7"]
    },
    {
      "text": "Corvale East has 2.6 days on hand at 3.5 vials per day, Corvale General has 14.4 days at 2.9 vials per day, and Corvale Lakeside has 26.5 days at 0.7 vials per day.",
      "cites": ["D1", "D2", "D3"]
    },
    {
      "text": "The top-ranked action is to transfer 8 vials of the 50 mg/mL 60 mL presentation from Corvale Lakeside to Corvale East, which would raise East to about 5 days on hand while Lakeside retains roughly two weeks.",
      "cites": ["D8"]
    },
    {
      "text": "P&T-approved alternatives include Hikma's 50 mg/mL vial (approved 2026-09-15) and Baxter's 1 g/20 mL vial (approved 2026-04-18), both requiring dose recalculation and pharmacist verification.",
      "cites": ["E13", "E14"]
    }
  ]
}
